=begin pod :page-card<Home> :nav-order<30>

=TITLE Sharing

=SUBTITLE Sharing your enthusiasm for Raku with others

So you enjoy Raku, and want to let others know about it?  There are a variety of 
ways you can do this.  

The L<marketing|https://marketing.raku.org/> site has some resources sorely in 
need of an update (talk to the L<Outreach Troupe|../troupes/outreach> to 
assist).  At this point, the only useful material is the logos, which you may be 
able to use in your efforts to share your love of Raku.  

=head1 Books/Merch/Financial Support

=item1 B<Books> don't directly support Raku itself, but they support other 
members of the Raku community,  Note that a number also refer to it as Perl 6, 
which is the old name.  

=item2 A few select books can be found at L<https://raku.org/learn>

=item2 A larger selection can be found at L<https://perl6book.com/>

=item2 Neither of the above lists includes 
L<Raku Recipes|https://www.amazon.com.au/Raku-Recipes-Problem-Solution-J-J-Merelo/dp/1484262573>

=item1 B<Merch>: You can also get some merch at 
L<Zazzle Raku/Rakudo Merch|https://www.zazzle.com/store/rakudo>.  

=item1 B<L<Donations|https://raku.foundation/Donations>> can be made to the Raku 
Foundation, which supports events, grants, and helps keep the Raku 
infrastructure running, 

=head1 Learning/Writing about Raku

Sometimes the best way to learn about something is to write about it,  You can 
read more about this approach on the L<Writing to Learn|sharing/writing-to-learn> 
page.  

=head1 Used in Production

Sometimes it can be useful in your sharing of Raku to be able to cite places 
where Raku has been used in production.  To that end, here's a list of places 
that that has been done:

